**Issue**: #417
**Date**: 2026-09-23
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Repair local project-provider verification failures without passing the gate
  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Explicit executed local project test failure returns to implementation
    Given a registered required applicable project provider executed a deterministic local test command
    And its exact-head complete-coverage artifact records a valid failed result with explicit repairability
    When the owning controller classifies the failed verification
    Then it routes to implementation remediation without converting the failed gate to pass

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Untrusted or incomplete evidence remains intervention
    Given a missing or malformed repairability field, readiness failure, missing credentials, external-only failure, incomplete prerequisite, stale head, or incomplete coverage
    When verification evaluates the evidence
    Then it refuses automatic implementation recovery
    And provider summary prose alone does not establish local execution

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Legacy failed artifact is eligible only by exact operator authorization
    Given the original pre-marker MileDar artifact is retained at the issue and head named by the operator
    And its bytes match the authorized digest and its request and result identities agree
    When the owning controller consumes the authorization once
    Then it preserves the failed report and artifact and resumes normal implementation
    And mismatched bytes or a second use cannot recover

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Recovery preserves all later gates and ownership
    Given a valid failed verify handoff with an exact owning head and one unused recovery
    When implementation remediation completes
    Then both review stages and every required verification gate run again
    And foreign owner, changed head, or repeated failure remains blocked
